course: dictionary
lesson: 657
title: Baggage: bags and burdens
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Baggage has two meanings, and context tells you which one is meant. In «Bags are tagged with barcodes and sent along kilometres of hidden belts to the right plane; nobody should ever climb on the baggage carousel», baggage means the bags and suitcases people take when they travel, because of the plane and the belts.
explain: Baggage is uncountable, so you do not say «a baggage» or «two baggages». You say «some baggage», «a lot of baggage» or «my bags».
explain: Sometimes baggage is a picture. «Emotional baggage» means worries, bad memories or old problems a person carries from the past. If a character has emotional baggage, the author is telling you that old hurts are still weighing them down, like a heavy suitcase.
explain: Ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. If you swap in «bags and suitcases» and it makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Baggage means the bags and suitcases you take when you travel.
fact: Baggage can also mean worries, bad memories or old problems carried from the past, as in «emotional baggage».
fact: Baggage is uncountable: say «some baggage» or «a lot of baggage», not «a baggage».
fact: Safety rule: never leave baggage unattended, and never carry a bag for a stranger.
fact: In «baggage reclaim» and «check in your baggage», the word is about airports and travel.
exercise: «Bags are tagged with barcodes and sent along kilometres of hidden belts to the right plane; nobody should ever climb on the baggage carousel.» What does baggage mean in this sentence? | Worries and bad memories from the past | A kind of aeroplane seat | *The bags and suitcases people take when they travel | Heavy boxes of books sent by post
exercise: Tom says his aunt has «emotional baggage» from an old argument. What does this mean? | Extra bags she bought for a holiday | *Old hurts and worries she still carries from the past | A large amount of money she has saved | A heavy suitcase full of books
exercise: Which is a safety rule about baggage? | Carry a bag for any stranger who asks you | *Never leave baggage unattended | Climb on the baggage carousel to find your bag | Hide your bag in a quiet corner
test: Which sentence is correct? | I have a baggage to carry. | I have baggages to carry. | I have two baggages to carry. | *I have a lot of baggage to carry.
test: In «sent along kilometres of hidden belts to the right plane», which word tells you baggage is about travel? | kilometres | *plane | barcodes | hidden
exam: «She still carries emotional baggage from her childhood.» What does this mean? | She forgot her passport on the trip | She packed too much for her holiday | She owns many suitcases from her childhood | *She still feels old hurts and worries from her childhood
